 14:24:34.960377	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
1109	16	1094	1	1	sale.order.template.form	sale.order.template	\N	form	sale_pdf_quote_builder/views/sale_order_template_views.xml	extension	{"en_US": "<notebook position=\\"inside\\">\\n                <page name=\\"pdf_quote\\" string=\\"PDF Quote Builder\\">\\n                    <group>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Provide header pages and footer pages to compose an attractive quotation\\n                            with more information about your company, your products and your services.\\n                            The pdf of your quotes will be built by putting together header pages,\\n                            product descriptions, details of the quote and then the footer pages.\\n                            If empty, it will use those define in the company settings.<br/>\\n                            <a href=\\"https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/_downloads/5f0840ed187116c425fdac2ab4b592e1/pdfquotebuilderexamples.zip\\">\\n                                <i class=\\"fa fa-arrow-right\\"/> Download examples\\n                            </a>\\n                        </p>\\n                        <group>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_header_name\\" invisible=\\"1\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_header\\" filename=\\"sale_header_name\\" options=\\"{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_footer_name\\" invisible=\\"1\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_footer\\" filename=\\"sale_footer_name\\" options=\\"{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}\\"/>\\n                        </group>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Products descriptions are pdf documents you can add directly on products.\\n                            To do so, go on a product, find the \\"product documents\\" button, then add a\\n                            new pdf document with a visibility set as \\"Inside Quotes\\". For each product\\n                            in the quote, if the product has an \\"inside quotes\\" document, this document\\n                            will be added after header pages and before the quotation details.\\n                        </p>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Some information specific to the quote (customer name, quotation reference, ... )\\n                            can be injected in these documents using pdf forms.\\n                            Refer to the documentation to know more about this feature.\\n                            <a href=\\"https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/applications/sales/sales/send_quotations/pdf_quote_builder.html\\">\\n                                Learn more from the documentation.\\n                            </a>\\n                        </p>\\n                    </group>\\n                </page>\\n            </notebook>", "es_AR": "<notebook position=\\"inside\\">\\n                <page name=\\"pdf_quote\\" string=\\"Creador de cotizaciones en PDF\\">\\n                    <group>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Cree encabezados y pies de páginas para crear una cotización llamativa\\n                            que tenga información sobre su empresa y los productos o servicios que ofrece.\\n                            Para crear el archivo PDF de sus cotizaciones se tomarán el encabezado,\\n                            las descripciones de los productos, los detalles de la cotización, los pies de página y se juntarán.\\n                            Si está vacío, usará lo que esté definido en los ajustes de la empresa.<br/>\\n                            <a href=\\"https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/_downloads/5f0840ed187116c425fdac2ab4b592e1/pdfquotebuilderexamples.zip\\">\\n                                <i class=\\"fa fa-arrow-right\\"/>Descargar ejemplos\\n                            </a>\\n                        </p>\\n                        <group>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_header_name\\" invisible=\\"1\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_header\\" filename=\\"sale_header_name\\" options=\\"{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_footer_name\\" invisible=\\"1\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"sale_footer\\" filename=\\"sale_footer_name\\" options=\\"{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}\\"/>\\n                        </group>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Las descripciones de productos son documentos PDF que puede agregar directamente a los productos.\\n                            Para hacerlo, vaya a un producto, busque el botón \\"documentos del producto\\" y agregue\\n                            un nuevo documento PDF con una visibilidad establecida como \\"Dentro de la cotización\\".\\n                            Si cada producto de la cotización tiene un documento \\"dentro de la cotización\\", este documento\\n                            se agregará después de las páginas de encabezado y antes de los detalles de la cotización.\\n                        </p>\\n                        <p class=\\"text-muted\\" colspan=\\"2\\">\\n                            Puede agregar información específica de a cotización (nombre del cliente,\\n                            referencia de la cotización, etc.) a estos documentos mediante formularios PDF.\\n                            Lea la documentación para obtener más información sobre esta función.\\n                            <a href=\\"https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/applications/sales/sales/send_quotations/pdf_quote_builder.html\\">\\n                                Consulta la documentación para obtener más información.\\n                            </a>\\n                        </p>\\n                    </group>\\n                </page>\\n            </notebook>"}	<?xml version="1.0"?>\n<notebook position="inside">\n                <page name="pdf_quote" string="PDF Quote Builder">\n                    <group>\n                        <p class="text-muted" colspan="2">\n                            Provide header pages and footer pages to compose an attractive quotation\n                            with more information about your company, your products and your services.\n                            The pdf of your quotes will be built by putting together header pages,\n                            product descriptions, details of the quote and then the footer pages.\n                            If empty, it will use those define in the company settings.<br/>\n                            <a href="https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/_downloads/5f0840ed187116c425fdac2ab4b592e1/pdfquotebuilderexamples.zip">\n                                <i class="fa fa-arrow-right"/> Download examples\n                            </a>\n                        </p>\n                        <group>\n                            <field name="sale_header_name" invisible="1"/>\n                            <field name="sale_header" filename="sale_header_name" options="{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}"/>\n                            <field name="sale_footer_name" invisible="1"/>\n                            <field name="sale_footer" filename="sale_footer_name" options="{'accepted_file_extensions': '.pdf'}"/>\n                        </group>\n                        <p class="text-muted" colspan="2">\n                            Products descriptions are pdf documents you can add directly on products.\n                            To do so, go on a product, find the "product documents" button, then add a\n                            new pdf document with a visibility set as "Inside Quotes". For each product\n                            in the quote, if the product has an "inside quotes" document, this document\n                            will be added after header pages and before the quotation details.\n                        </p>\n                        <p class="text-muted" colspan="2">\n                            Some information specific to the quote (customer name, quotation reference, ... )\n                            can be injected in these documents using pdf forms.\n                            Refer to the documentation to know more about this feature.\n                            <a href="https://www.odoo.com/documentation/17.0/applications/sales/sales/send_quotations/pdf_quote_builder.html">\n                                Learn more from the documentation.\n                            </a>\n                        </p>\n                    </group>\n                </page>\n            </notebook>\n        	f	t	2026-10-30 14:24:36.555909	2026-10-30 14:24:36.555909	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
1111	16	\N	1	1	Barcode Nomenclatures	barcode.nomenclature	\N	form	barcodes/views/barcodes_view.xml	primary	{"en_US": "<form string=\\"Barcode Nomenclature\\">\\n                    <sheet>\\n                        <group name=\\"general_attributes\\" col=\\"4\\">\\n                            <field name=\\"name\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"upc_ean_conv\\"/>\\n                        </group>\\n                        <div>\\n                            <p>\\n                                <i>Barcodes Nomenclatures</i> define how barcodes are recognized and categorized.\\n                                When a barcode is scanned it is associated to the <i>first</i> rule with a matching\\n                                pattern. The pattern syntax is that of regular expression, and a barcode is matched\\n                                if the regular expression matches a prefix of the barcode.\\n                            </p><p>\\n                                Patterns can also define how numerical values, such as weight or price, can be\\n                                encoded into the barcode. They are indicated by <code>{NNN}</code> where the N's\\n                                define where the number's digits are encoded. Floats are also supported with the\\n                                decimals indicated with D's, such as <code>{NNNDD}</code>. In these cases,\\n                                the barcode field on the associated records <i>must</i> show these digits as\\n                                zeroes.\\n                            </p>\\n                        </div>\\n                        <field name=\\"rule_ids\\">\\n                            <tree string=\\"Tables\\">\\n                                <field name=\\"sequence\\" widget=\\"handle\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"name\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"type\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"encoding\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"pattern\\"/>\\n                            </tree>\\n                        </field>\\n                    </sheet>\\n                </form>", "es_AR": "<form string=\\"Nomenclatura del código de barras\\">\\n                    <sheet>\\n                        <group name=\\"general_attributes\\" col=\\"4\\">\\n                            <field name=\\"name\\"/>\\n                            <field name=\\"upc_ean_conv\\"/>\\n                        </group>\\n                        <div>\\n                            <p>\\n                                Las <i>nomenclaturas de códigos de barras</i> definen cómo se reconocen y categorizan estos códigos.\\n                                Al escanear un código de barras, se asocia con la <i>primera</i> regla que tenga un patrón\\n                                coincidente. La sintaxis del patrón es la de una expresión regular, y un código de barras coincide\\n                                si la expresión regular coincide con el prefijo de un código de barras.\\n                            </p><p>\\n                                Los patrones también pueden definir el modo en que los valores numéricos, como el peso o el precio, se\\n                                codifican en el código de barras. Estos se indican con <code>{NNN}</code>, donde las N\\n                                definen dónde se codifican los dígitos del número. También se admiten valores decimales con\\n                                D, como en <code>{NNNDD}</code>. En estos casos,\\n                                el campo del código de barras en los registros asociados <i>debe</i> mostrar estos dígitos como\\n                                ceros.\\n                            </p>\\n                        </div>\\n                        <field name=\\"rule_ids\\">\\n                            <tree string=\\"Tablas\\">\\n                                <field name=\\"sequence\\" widget=\\"handle\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"name\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"type\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"encoding\\"/>\\n                                <field name=\\"pattern\\"/>\\n                            </tree>\\n                        </field>\\n                    </sheet>\\n                </form>"}	<?xml version="1.0"?>\n<form string="Barcode Nomenclature">\n                    <sheet>\n                        <group name="general_attributes" col="4">\n                            <field name="name"/>\n                            <field name="upc_ean_conv"/>\n                        </group>\n                        <div>\n                            <p>\n                                <i>Barcodes Nomenclatures</i> define how barcodes are recognized and categorized.\n                                When a barcode is scanned it is associated to the <i>first</i> rule with a matching\n                                pattern. The pattern syntax is that of regular expression, and a barcode is matched\n                                if the regular expression matches a prefix of the barcode.\n                            </p><p>\n                                Patterns can also define how numerical values, such as weight or price, can be\n                                encoded into the barcode. They are indicated by <code>{NNN}</code> where the N's\n                                define where the number's digits are encoded. Floats are also supported with the\n                                decimals indicated with D's, such as <code>{NNNDD}</code>. In these cases,\n                                the barcode field on the associated records <i>must</i> show these digits as\n                                zeroes.\n                            </p>\n                        </div>\n                        <field name="rule_ids">\n                            <tree string="Tables">\n                                <field name="sequence" widget="handle"/>\n                                <field name="name"/>\n                                <field name="type"/>\n                                <field name="encoding"/>\n                                <field name="pattern"/>\n                            </tree>\n                        </field>\n                    </sheet>\n                </form>\n            	f	t	2026-10-30 14:36:03.038956	2026-10-30 14:36:03.038956	f	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N
